1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,822
Every fifteen minutes,

2
00:00:01,822 --> 00:00:05,067
a state grid is billed for every megawatt it misses.

3
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:05,941
This is ADRMS:

4
00:00:05,941 --> 00:00:07,938
demand response, run end to end.

5
00:00:09,487 --> 00:00:11,508
It watches the grid every second:

6
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,345
frequency, area control error,

7
00:00:13,345 --> 00:00:15,611
and the deviation charge building up.

8
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:18,166
When a shortfall opens,

9
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:21,178
it explains the situation and proposes a plan,

10
00:00:21,178 --> 00:00:22,356
in plain language.

11
00:00:23,406 --> 00:00:25,654
The plan follows a strict priority.

12
00:00:25,654 --> 00:00:28,543
Batteries first. Then industrial flexibility.

13
00:00:28,543 --> 00:00:29,891
Then everything else.

14
00:00:30,941 --> 00:00:33,929
Every megawatt is tracked as planned versus measured,

15
00:00:33,929 --> 00:00:36,296
because an instruction is not a reduction.

16
00:00:37,347 --> 00:00:39,194
Before anything is dispatched,

17
00:00:39,194 --> 00:00:42,397
a digital twin screens the plan against line limits,

18
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:44,429
battery charge and response time.

19
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,591
Industries take part through offers,

20
00:00:47,591 --> 00:00:48,765
on their own window,

21
00:00:48,765 --> 00:00:50,173
response time and price.

22
00:00:51,223 --> 00:00:54,332
Delivery is verified against a metered baseline,

23
00:00:54,332 --> 00:00:56,471
and only verified energy is paid.

24
00:00:57,521 --> 00:00:59,320
Only what is left is rotated:

25
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:01,058
fairly, within spell limits,

26
00:01:01,058 --> 00:01:03,354
keeping hospitals and water works on,

27
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:05,030
and never without approval.

28
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:08,686
Operators can test any shortage first:

29
00:01:08,686 --> 00:01:10,675
no action, flexibility first,

30
00:01:10,675 --> 00:01:11,499
or rotation.

31
00:01:12,549 --> 00:01:16,282
Afterwards, every event settles against a counterfactual ledger,

32
00:01:16,282 --> 00:01:18,266
with a tamper-evident audit trail.

33
00:01:19,316 --> 00:01:20,800
ADRMS. Batteries first,

34
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,671
industry next, rotation last,

35
00:01:22,671 --> 00:01:24,542
with the operator in control.

